.TH MASTEROPS 1 "September 2026" "v0.1.4" "MasterOps User Manual"
.SH NAME
masterops \t DevOps bootstrap CLI for infrastructure and application environments.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B masterops
\fI[COMMAND]\fR
\fI[OPTIONS]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
MasterOps is a DevOps bootstrap tool designed to provision real, production-ready application environments on Linux servers. It handles the installation of runtimes, dependencies, services, and web servers (Nginx) in a modular and idempotent way.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B start \fI<project>\fR
Bootstrap a new framework project (e.g., .NET, Spring Boot, Laravel, Django, Go).
.TP
.B status
Show system-wide and project-specific health and configuration.
.TP
.B diff \fI<project>\fR
Detect configuration and environment drift between the desired state and the actual system.
.TP
.B audit
Run a comprehensive security audit of the server and deployed projects.
.TP
.B backup
Trigger an immediate S3 backup of all projects and configuration.
.TP
.B vault \fI<cmd>\fR
Manage encrypted project secrets using AES-256.
.TP
.B upgrade \fI<project>\fR
Upgrade project configuration version and apply migrations.
.TP
.B terraform \fI--start\fR
Provision AWS infrastructure (VPC, EC2, S3) via Terraform.
.TP
.B nginx \fI--start\fR
Configure Nginx for the server.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Display the help message for a command.
.TP
.B -v, --version
Display the MasterOps version.
.SH EXAMPLES
.B Create a new project:
.IP
masterops start my-app
.B Check system health:
.IP
masterops status
.B Detect drift in a project:
.IP
masterops diff my-app
.B Run security audit:
.IP
masterops audit
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/masterops/state.yaml
Global system state registry.
.TP
.B /var/www/\fI<project>\fR/.masterops/state.yaml
Project-specific state and configuration.
.TP
.B /var/log/masterops/masterops.log
Structured JSON logs for all operations.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success.
.TP
1
Drift detected or a non-critical error occurred.
.TP
2
Invalid arguments or a critical error occurred.
.SH AUTHOR
Developed by MoTarek @ DevOpsEngineer.
